<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <!-- CSS Assets -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/output.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/app.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/w3.css" />

    <!-- Javascript Assets -->
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/doc@latest/dist/doc.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/doc@latest/dist/doc.min.js"></script>
    <script src="../js/app.js" defer></script>
    <script src="../js/jquery.js"></script>
    <style>
      h2 {
        font-weight: 800;
      }
      li {
        margin-top: 5px;
        padding-left: 5px;
      }

      .drop-area {
        border: 2px dashed #ccc;
        height: 50px;
        margin-top: 10px;
      }
      .item.dragging :where(.details, i) {
        opacity: 0;
      }
      .hoverDash {
        border-style: dashed;
        border-width: 2px; /* Adjust the width of the border */
        border-spacing: 6px; /* Adjust the spacing between dashes */
      }
      .draggable-container {
        transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-100vh text-black bg-slate-50">
    <div class="header bg-white px-2 py-6 border w-full rounded font-semibold">
      Blazing Share Zoom Integration Guide
    </div>

    <div class="content px-3">
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to the Blazing Share Zoom Integration Guide! This guide will
        walk you through adding, using, and removing the Blazing Share Zoom
        integration.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Adding the Blazing Share Zoom App</h2>
      <p>To add Blazing Share to Zoom:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Navigate to the Zoom App Marketplace and search for "Blazing Share".
        </li>
        <li>
          Click on the Blazing Share app, select Install, review permissions,
          and click Authorize.
        </li>
        <li>
          After installation, sign in to Blazing Share to link it with Zoom.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>3. Using the Blazing Share App with Zoom</h2>
      <h3>A. Setting Up Backups</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Enable Automatic Backup in Blazing Share under Settings > Integrations
          > Zoom.
        </li>
        <li>
          Manually Backup Zoom Recordings by selecting recordings and clicking
          "Backup to Google Drive".
        </li>
        <li>Customize Backup Locations under Settings > Storage.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>B. Viewing Backed Up Recordings</h3>
      <p>
        Access backed-up recordings through Blazing Share or your designated
        Google Drive folder.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Removing the Blazing Share Zoom App</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Visit the Zoom App Marketplace, go to Installed Apps, and uninstall
          Blazing Share.
        </li>
        <li>
          In Blazing Share, disable permissions under Settings > Integrations >
          Zoom if needed.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>5. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div>
        <div class="accordion-item" onclick="toggleAccordion(1)">
          <p>Q: What permissions are required?</p>
        </div>
        <div id="accordion-content-1" class="accordion-content">
          <p class="ml-4 text-gray-600">
            A: Blazing Share requires access to your Zoom recordings and user
            information to transfer files to Google Drive.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item" onclick="toggleAccordion(2)">
          <p>Q: How do I contact support?</p>
        </div>
        <div id="accordion-content-2" class="accordion-content">
          <p class="ml-4 text-gray-600">
            A: For support, email support@yourdomain.com or visit our Support
            Page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
